tool_a.code_example:
// Cursor's agent works on the open repository, so the unit of work
// is a task, not a suggestion. The bill follows the model you route to.
// .cursor/rules/backend.mdc — project rules apply to every agent run
---
description: Backend conventions
globs: services/**/*.py
---
Never edit migrations by hand; generate them and review the diff.
// Here it breaks: on Premium, requests routed to Claude or GPT are billed
// at API list price separately from the $30 subscription — watch the invoice,
// not just the seat count.

